\begin{abstract}
We present a real-time, stability-certified multi-scale simulation architecture
that integrates astrophysical tensor fields with genetic blueprint dynamics.
Operating on a 64-node NVIDIA HGX H100 cluster, the system enforces Lyapunov
stability, sector dominance, and Control Barrier Function (CBF) constraints using
live telemetry from ingestion bandwidth, tensor core utilization, ring-buffer
latency, and Jacobian determinants. Closed-form expressions for stability
parameters $(\alpha, \beta, c_d, \gamma)$ are derived directly from hardware
metrics, proving global asymptotic stability within the safe operating region
$\mathcal{R}_{\text{safe}}$. Stress testing demonstrates that the architecture
maintains provable stability under extreme burst telemetry and near-singular
manifold deformation.
\end{abstract}

